not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-056270","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001529113","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1529113/000121390026056270/ea0289941-10q_xtiaero.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2.bin","sha256":"2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2"}},{"id":"703389536e63bf946aae07685c7af49d2b8c9073f3617ac9e61eb180e6b4e678","quote":"On February 3, 2026 (the “Signing Date” and “Closing Date”), the Company completed the disposition of its Inpixon Business pursuant to a Share Purchase and Transfer Agreement (the “SPA”) entered into with EVO 467. GmbH (the “Purchaser”). Pursuant to the SPA, the Company sold all of the shares of Inpixon GmbH for a purchase price of EUR 4,640,000 (approximately $5.5 million based on the exchange rate on the Signing Date).","context":"Disposition of the Inpixon Business","section":"The following tables reflect the results of operations from our business segments for the periods indicated below (in thousands):","block":372,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-056270","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001529113","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1529113/000121390026056270/ea0289941-10q_xtiaero.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2.bin","sha256":"2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2"}},{"id":"2f0f6b7682c051d06ac6a66a7f4c3cd25b6b7cbb2f4cd46e1695f998ba5ba619","quote":"Inpixon GmbH is the sole shareholder of Aware RTLS, Inc. and IntraNav GmbH. The Inpixon Business, which provides indoor positioning, real-time localization and sensor technology solutions, was conducted through Inpixon GmbH.","context":"On February 3, 2026 (the “Signing Date” and “Closing Date”), the Company completed the disposition of its Inpixon Business pursuant to a Share Purchase and Transfer Agreement (the “SPA”) entered into with EVO 467. GmbH (the “Purchaser”). Pursuant to the SPA, the Company sold all of the shares of Inpixon GmbH for a purchase price of EUR 4,640,000 (approximately $5.5 million based on the exchange rate on the Signing Date).","section":"The following tables reflect the results of operations from our business segments for the periods indicated below (in thousands):","block":373,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-056270","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001529113","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1529113/000121390026056270/ea0289941-10q_xtiaero.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2.bin","sha256":"2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2"}},{"id":"e1ae8b7d162b266cd77f29c851ba5441e03c9a9ed632e51e3ff5ed0e81815364","quote":"The purchase price of EUR 4,640,000 bears interest of 5% per annum from the Signing Date until the fourth anniversary of the Closing Date. The Company has the right (the “Unwind Option”) to require the Purchaser to transfer back all shares of Inpixon and its subsidiaries at any time during that fifteen (15) month period beginning on the first day of the thirty-seventh month following the Signing Date and continuing to the end of the fifty-second month following the Signing Date for no consideration by the Company. If exercised, all unpaid amounts of the purchase price will be forgiven. If not exercised within the specified period, the unpaid purchase price will also be forgiven.","context":"Inpixon GmbH is the sole shareholder of Aware RTLS, Inc. and IntraNav GmbH. The Inpixon Business, which provides indoor positioning, real-time localization and sensor technology solutions, was conducted through Inpixon GmbH.","section":"The following tables reflect the results of operations from our business segments for the periods indicated below (in thousands):","block":374,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-056270","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001529113","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1529113/000121390026056270/ea0289941-10q_xtiaero.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2.bin","sha256":"2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2"}},{"id":"e32fee94fd5dc5e4a1c9cb28dd1b435d79a51dd9ce7c83d78b21e20a3c7bfe26","quote":"NOTES TO CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS","context":"XTI AEROSPACE, INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES","section":"The following tables reflect the results of operations from our business segments for the periods indicated below (in thousands):","block":377,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-056270","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001529113","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1529113/000121390026056270/ea0289941-10q_xtiaero.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2.bin","sha256":"2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2"}},{"id":"3a47b92e998e95c7a97cafb538cca42cb0edabd428f1f84c007e632dbe43fc9e","quote":"The Company evaluated the Unwind Option in accordance with ASC 810-10-40, Consolidation—Deconsolidation, and concluded that control of the Inpixon Business transferred to the Purchaser upon closing. Based on management’s evaluation of the facts and circumstances surrounding the transaction, including the Purchaser’s business plan and other qualitative considerations, the likelihood of exercise of the Unwind Option is considered remote. Additionally, the purchase price terms, including the potential forgiveness provisions, were also considered in the Company’s assessment of whether the transaction qualified for sale accounting. Finally, the Company has no continuing involvement in the operations of the Inpixon Business following the Closing Date. Accordingly, the transaction was accounted for as a complete sale and the Inpixon Business was derecognized as of the Closing Date.","context":"NOTES TO CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS","section":"The following tables reflect the results of operations from our business segments for the periods indicated below (in thousands):","block":378,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-056270","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001529113","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1529113/000121390026056270/ea0289941-10q_xtiaero.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2.bin","sha256":"2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2"}},{"id":"37ad7edc7cb8e6b66d90d9e86aad73349e3cf97d28e8daa2b6b908a2db24836e","quote":"The Company recorded the purchase price as a note receivable with fair value determined to be $4.2 million, as of the Closing Date, in the accompanying unaudited condensed consolidated balance sheets. As discussed above, the note receivable accrues interest at 5% per annum and matures on February 3, 2030. Subject to provisions discussed related to the Unwind Option, the note receivable may be forgiven. The Company determined the fair value of the note receivable based on the perceived credit risk of the counterparty and time value of money, going forward the note receivable will be evaluated for risk of credit loss and will not be remeasured.","context":"The Company evaluated the Unwind Option in accordance with ASC 810-10-40, Consolidation—Deconsolidation, and concluded that control of the Inpixon Business transferred to the Purchaser upon closing. Based on management’s evaluation of the facts and circumstances surrounding the transaction, including the Purchaser’s business plan and other qualitative considerations, the likelihood of exercise of the Unwind Option is considered remote. Additionally, the purchase price terms, including the potential forgiveness provisions, were also considered in the Company’s assessment of whether the transaction qualified for sale accounting. Finally, the Company has no continuing involvement in the operations of the Inpixon Business following the Closing Date. Accordingly, the transaction was accounted for as a complete sale and the Inpixon Business was derecognized as of the Closing Date.","section":"The following tables reflect the results of operations from our business segments for the periods indicated below (in thousands):","block":379,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-056270","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001529113","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1529113/000121390026056270/ea0289941-10q_xtiaero.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2.bin","sha256":"2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2"}},{"id":"bd4f1bd8a5b3c4e6fc777c798b52c9f1657bfb892caf51335f96dc0af22a57e4","quote":"The following table presents the results of discontinued operations for the three months ended March 31, 2026 and 2025 (in thousands):","context":"Results of Discontinued Operations","section":"The following tables reflect the results of operations from our business segments for the periods indicated below (in thousands):","block":381,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_ver