 including the Drone Nerds acquisition and working capital stabilization. During the three months ended March 31, 2026, we received approximately $7.4 million in net proceeds from the exercise of warrants and entered into a $20.0 million asset-based revolving credit facility, subject to a borrowing base. The Company ended the most recent quarter with cash on hand of $15.2 million and $16.7 million as of March 31, 2026 and December 31, 2025. Our operating priorities are focused on:","context":"Capital Allocation and Liquidity Strategy","section":"ITEM 2: MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":434,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-056270","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001529113","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1529113/000121390026056270/ea0289941-10q_xtiaero.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2.bin","sha256":"2cca18decf248f28be4490e1f5a7801ca41ac79ae24de5ddd740be1f278b65e2"}},{"id":"21ea32a4815ceed9260fbd1ca940a21f602e031d5f0e068df4b5eea15e5461d9","quote":"This increase was due primarily to increased personnel-related expenses, including stock-based compensation, and operating expenses incurred at the Drone Nerds business which was acquired in the fourth quarter of 2025 and therefore has no activity reflected in the three months ended March 31, 2025.","context":"Operating expenses for the three months ended March 31, 2026 were $15.5 million, an increase of $7.3 million, or 89%, compared to $8.2 million for the comparable period ended March 31, 2025.","section":"RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":471,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-056270","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-14","reportDate":"20